# A name declared inside an `L2:` record belongs to the lexical branch of the record and is not seen after it (the book, section 3: «Новое
# локальное имя ветви видно на её уровне и во вложенных ветвях, но не снаружи»). The read of `inner` after the record resolves to nothing:
# the run answers 3, as for any name that resolves to nothing (the row closed_data_missing pins 3).
fn: outer () int (int: total 0)
    L2:
        int: inner 40
    total := inner
    return: total
int: result outer()
